From: vps-ssh-launcher maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Fail a truncated workbuddy stream instead of reporting it complete

Source: mmqz/cpa-multi-plugins v0.8.78 (MIT); workbuddy 0.9.64. Mirrors the
accepted upstream fix for the sibling qoder plugin (upstream issue/PR #48,
"stop reporting a truncated stream as a complete answer").
Apply after workbuddy-v0.8.68-selected-account.patch and
workbuddy-v0.8.68-account-failover.patch, using git apply --recount.
Consumer: BWG CPA v8.0.38 + workbuddy 0.9.64-local (2026-10-22).
Retire when upstream ships the same termination witness for workbuddy.

Why: pumpUpstreamStream treated a 200 stream that delivered frames and then
ended cleanly as a success. With no finish_reason and no [DONE] the client is
left holding half an answer. The qoder plugin already fixed exactly this;
workbuddy never got the guard (0.9.64 still lacks sawFinish/sawTerminator).

Wording: "truncated_stream: ... (unexpected EOF)" keeps the failure in the
transport-lifecycle family CPA's cooldown classifier already understands, so a
cut upstream never cools a healthy credential.

diff --git a/plugins/workbuddy/policy.go b/plugins/workbuddy/policy.go
index efb00a6..1e48c74 100755
--- a/plugins/workbuddy/policy.go
+++ b/plugins/workbuddy/policy.go
@@ -163,6 +163,15 @@ func emptyStreamError() error {
 	return fmt.Errorf("empty_stream: workbuddy upstream closed before a completion payload (unexpected EOF)")
 }
 
+// truncatedStreamError is the half-answer twin of emptyStreamError: the upstream
+// answered, then stopped before any finish_reason/[DONE]. Same transport
+// lifecycle wording, so the classifier must not cool a credential that is
+// perfectly healthy; the difference is that frames were already delivered, and
+// without this the client would take the partial text as the model's last word.
+func truncatedStreamError() error {
+	return fmt.Errorf("truncated_stream: workbuddy upstream ended without finish_reason (unexpected EOF)")
+}
+
